{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdHQubpkwgSJCUenLDvb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the job and written up the causes in `ANSWER.md`. It has been running every night (`runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1`), but it fails each time, and three bugs together keep anything from reaching you:\n\n1. **`claude -p` stops with \"Not logged in\".** Under launchd it can't find your login, because the plist sets only `PATH` (no `USER`) and your keychain may be locked at 02:30.\n2. **`status=$?` kills the script.** In zsh, `status` is a read-only variable, so line 19 aborts the script before it sends the failure message. That's why you got nothing at all, not even a failure note.\n3. **`notify.sh` would have failed too.** It gets the bot token from the keychain, which is locked at night, and `set -e` then exits before the message is sent. It never read `config.toml`, the file you set up for exactly this case.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- **Script:** uses `rc=$?` instead of `status`, gives `claude` a closed stdin (`< /dev/null`), saves its errors to a file, and treats empty output as a failure. The failure message now includes the start of the error.\n- **Notifier:** tries the keychain first, then falls back to the token in `config.toml`. If it finds neither, it prints a clear error.\n- **Plist:** adds `USER=vk` and puts `~/.local/bin` on `PATH`.\n- **`config.toml`:** set so only you can read it (`chmod 600`).\n\nThe syntax checks pass for all three files. In a test run with fake `claude`, `security` and `curl`, a failed review now sends \"nightly review FAILED (exit 1): Not logged in\", and the notifier picks up the token from `config.toml` when the keychain fails. Nothing has run under launchd or sent a real Telegram message yet.\n\n**What you need to do** (I didn't touch your live system):\n- **Reload the agent:** run `launchctl bootout`, then `bootstrap` again. Then trigger a run with `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review` and check that a Telegram message arrives and today's review file isn't empty.\n- **If it still says \"Not logged in\":** run `claude setup-token`, store the token in a file only you can read, and have the script export it as `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Don't put it in the plist.\n- **Security:** `README.md` has a Telegram bot token in plain text and isn't git-ignored. Remove it and revoke it with @BotFather. Also keep this job from loading `~/.env`, which holds your Stripe, AWS and database secrets; the review doesn't need them.\n\nAs you asked, I checked worklore first. One story (\"zsh killed the messenger\") matched this exact pattern, and it also suggested the `USER` and `< /dev/null` fixes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1641,"cache_read_input_tokens":30431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1641},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4994292f-b066-43bc-b6fb-e3924ef9435f","uuid":"8fb86c9c-b23b-4183-88d6-1f7593cdd97a","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:06:40.119Z","request_id":"req_011CgdHQuLwjzjXX3GVwrR15"}
